#: honoka-internal-link-audit.php:514
msgid "Only published posts are read. Pages, drafts, attachments and other post types are left out."
msgstr ""

#: honoka-internal-link-audit.php:515
msgid "Each post is measured after the content filters run, so shortcodes and blocks are counted the way a visitor sees them. Text inside HTML comments is not counted, because it is not on the page."
msgstr ""

#: honoka-internal-link-audit.php:516
msgid "An internal link is a link to this same site. Links starting with tel:, mailto: or # are not internal links. A link from a post to itself does not count as a link to it."
msgstr ""

#: honoka-internal-link-audit.php:517
msgid "alt=\"\" is correct markup for a decorative image and is not reported as missing. Only an img tag with no alt attribute at all is."
msgstr ""

#: honoka-internal-link-audit.php:518
msgid "Link targets are resolved with WordPress' own url_to_postid(), so a link written before a slug or category change still counts for the post it now points to."
msgstr ""

